## Reviewer points not applied as written

- Space as the thousands separator is right for Finnish and wrong for this checker. Not applied (fi-a 47, fi-b 23).
- Turning Q16–Q20 into headings, and deleting U+200B lines, would change heading levels or block counts against the English source. Not applied (fi-a 44).
- Deleting the Difficulty row would drop a table row the English article still has. Not applied (fi-a 49); the cells were reworded instead.
- Spelling "1", "3", "4" and "6" out as words would drop digits the checker counts. Digits kept.
- "oikeussubjektius" is the right Finnish term for legal personality. It was not swept into "taho". Only the responsible-entity calque "subjekti" was.
- fi-b 13 was applied to match English ("The foregoing is contract-design advice"), even though that English sentence sits under the branch-versus-subsidiary procedure and is an odd fit. The Finnish denial was the mistranslation; the English meaning was restored.
